## Presets and optional infrastructure

The fullstack preset is the default. Presets are starting points; required
companions are added automatically:

```bash
# Fullstack SaaS: Postgres + Better Auth + Zustand
smokeforge new ./app --kind frontend --stack next --name "App" --preset fullstack

# Frontend only
smokeforge new ./app --kind frontend --stack next --name "App" --preset frontend

# Production: fullstack + Docker + CI + E2E + PostHog
smokeforge new ./app --kind frontend --stack next --name "App" --preset production
```

Individual overlays can be added with `--feature` or `smokeforge add`. For
example, `--feature docker --feature ci:github` brings the required E2E overlay
with CI.

### Docker

The `docker` overlay adds:

- `Dockerfile` — package-manager-aware multi-stage build; non-root runtime.
- `.dockerignore`
- `compose.yaml` — app service using `.env` and a health check.
- `make docker-build`, `make docker-up`, `make docker-down`.

The database overlay adds `compose.override.yaml`, so `make docker-up`
automatically starts Postgres alongside the app. Run migrations explicitly; the
app does not migrate on boot.

### Analytics

The `analytics:posthog` overlay adds privacy-first PostHog bootstrap:
autocapture and session recording off, memory persistence, and no capture until
`optInAnalytics()` from `@/lib/analytics/consent` is called.

### CI

The `ci:github` overlay adds `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, which installs with the
selected package manager, then runs lint, typecheck, Jest, build, and Playwright.
CI requires the E2E overlay, which is added automatically.

Commit the lockfile so CI can use frozen installs. The workflow falls back to a
normal install before a lockfile exists.

